{"id": "EUVD-2026-55436", "enisaUuid": "f02bf97f-c14b-3ff0-9cb1-4dcf08974c03", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrds: drop incoming messages that cross network namespace boundaries\n\nrds_find_bound() looks up the destination socket using a global\nrhashtable keyed solely on (addr, port, scope_id).  Network namespaces\nare not part of the key, so a sender in netns A can deliver an incoming\nmessage (inc) to a socket that lives in a different netns B.\n\nWhen this happens, inc->i_conn points to an rds_connection whose c_net\nis netns A, but the receiving rs lives in netns B.  Once the child\nprocess that created netns A exits, cleanup_net() calls\nrds_loop_exit_net() -> rds_loop_kill_conns() -> rds_conn_destroy(),\nfreeing that connection.  If the survivor socket in netns B still holds\nthe inc, any subsequent dereference of inc->i_conn is a use-after-free.\n\nThere are two dangerous sites in rds_clear_recv_queue():\n  1. inc->i_conn->c_lcong (offset 88 of freed rds_connection, size 200)\n     read via rds_recv_rcvbuf_delta() -- confirmed by KASAN.\n  2. inc->i_conn->c_trans->inc_free(inc) (function pointer at offset 80)\n     called via rds_inc_put() when the inc refcount reaches zero -- same\n     race window, potential call-through-freed-object primitive.\n\nThe bug is reachable from unprivileged user namespaces\n(CLONE_NEWUSER + CLONE_NEWNET), available since Linux 3.8.\n\nFix this by rejecting the delivery in rds_recv_incoming() when the\nsocket returned by rds_find_bound() belongs to a different network\nnamespace than the connection that carried the message.  Use the\nexisting rds_conn_net() / sock_net() helpers and net_eq() for the\ncomparison.", "datePublished": "2026-08-10T12:03:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T21:09:05", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/742ff6f02545212e991cd8b45011e40d2c2ef25a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abff41fd928328bbf3dda1140beb2e61fa424ccd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03c574112e5d066df0ddce36d7438e850bcf3050", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e2e2d9806944fe485824d617c8b7c78116c22db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfb3ce07b705e486e022a2f2b1242b48f13981ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9591042533140dfe6608d9344806d567dcd39d02", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f8690e3869109cd5803ccb400889d20a0b54e0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5521ae71e32a8069ed4ca6e792179dc57bc43ab2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-c7h5-q22g-86gx", "CVE-2026-68335"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b75380b-dbc4-33c2-b8a5-243acc72b1cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c809195f5523dd4d09403bbb1c9732d548aa0d1e <742ff6f02545212e991cd8b45011e40d2c2ef25a"}, {"id": "1ca46078-c3ca-3ae6-b149-c4dc8903e636", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "2960ae1e-92b3-30c1-9f39-49392952a06b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "2aa25f96-894e-3aa7-8c0b-f86df5eb6f57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "304e121c-8569-3497-9422-895054a7d448", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.265"}, {"id": "4eb0fbde-4468-3c03-9379-7d013a03028c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.17.19 <4.18"}, {"id": "5830486f-8dbe-3a07-a4b9-737c9cbdc492", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c809195f5523dd4d09403bbb1c9732d548aa0d1e <03c574112e5d066df0ddce36d7438e850bcf3050"}, {"id": "58da7f82-0383-3c7e-8553-6316ca41a373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}, {"id": "641711a9-280e-33b6-9cf9-b3f3c4392803", "produ